cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "crystal-bci: crystallization-learned templates for fail-closed biosignal commands (synthetic)"
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/crystal-bci"
keywords:
  - synthetic-biosignal
  - hebbian-learning
  - spike-triggered-average
  - fail-closed-gate
  - brain-computer-interface
  - classical-simulation
abstract: >-
  Applies the membrane-crystallization findings to biosignal
  commands: a peak-triggered Hebbian learner extracts a blink
  template (the crystal) unsupervised from a noisy synthetic
  multichannel stream, and a Youden-calibrated fail-closed gate
  turns blinks into a 'next' command. Measured: cosine 0.784
  with the true direction, hit rate 1.000 with 0 false alarms,
  learned crystal beats a fixed template 1.000/0 vs 0.765/114.
  Synthetic signals only; not a medical device; the device-data
  adapter to real recordings is still missing.
